# XSH toupper() and toupper_l()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The tests run in the POSIX locale (setlocale(LC_ALL, "C")); only the
# portable character set is examined. The _l forms are tested with a locale
# object from newlocale() for "C"; a failure to make one is UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XSH.toupper.001
anchor     functions/toupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/toupper.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
class      required
since      1988
says       In the POSIX locale toupper() maps each of the 26 lowercase letters
           to the 26 uppercase letters at the same place of the alphabet, as
           the locale definition pairs them. Checked through the function and
           through the header form.
test       t/001-letters.c

assertion  XSH.toupper.002
anchor     functions/toupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/toupper.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
class      required
since      1988
says       In the POSIX locale toupper() returns every other portable character
           unchanged: the 26 uppercase letters, the ten digits, the space, the
           32 punctuation characters and the portable control characters
           including the null character.
note       Only portable characters are examined.
test       t/002-unchanged.c

assertion  XSH.toupper.003
anchor     functions/toupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/toupper.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       toupper(EOF) is inside the domain and returns EOF.
test       t/003-eof.c

assertion  XSH.toupper.004
anchor     functions/toupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/toupper.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
class      required
since      2008
says       toupper_l() with a locale object for the POSIX locale maps each of
           the 26 lowercase letters to the 26 uppercase letters at the same
           place of the alphabet.
note       The locale object comes from newlocale(); UNRESOLVED if it cannot be
           made.
test       t/004-locale-object.c

assertion  XSH.toupper.005
anchor     functions/toupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/toupper.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2008
says       toupper_l() with a locale object for the POSIX locale returns every
           other portable character and EOF unchanged.
test       t/005-locale-unchanged.c

assertion  XSH.toupper.006
anchor     functions/toupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/toupper.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
class      required
since      1988
says       Converting a letter with toupper() and then back with tolower()
           gives the original letter, for each of the 26 lowercase letters;
           likewise through the _l forms.
note       A consequence of the two POSIX-locale conversion tables, which are
           inverse to each other.
test       t/006-round-trip.c
